//// Decision 441 (144 B-00e; its cell waited on B-00k for decision 457's
//// per-target answer, 144 B-29 step H): `trim` removes std-wasm's whitespace
//// set — space, tab, LF, CR, VT, FF — and a NBSP (U+00A0) stays, on wasm,
//// erlang and beam. commonJS's `trim` is the JS engine's, which removes the
//// NBSP too, and departs.

pub fn main() {
    val s = "\u{a0}x\u{a0} ";
    @print("[" + s.trim() + "]");
}
